  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up interventions to combat malaria in Cote d&apos;Ivorie in the context of National reconstruction - C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire (01-Jan-2012-30-Jun-2015)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire is a country where Malaria is an endemic. Malaria is assessed as the foremost cause of morbidity and of mortality in the hospital. Pregnant women and children under five are most significantly affected populations. The Round 9 proposal supports the Strategic National Plan for 2006 to 2010 in scaling up Malaria interventions from 19 districts currently covered to the whole country and achieving universal access. The Program is implemented through the dual-track financing scheme by two Principal Recipients (PR).  The activities undertaken by this PR include long-lasting insecticidal nets (LLIN) mass distribution campaign and information, education, and behavior change communication to support increased intermittent preventive therapy (IPT) and proper insecticide-treated net use.</narrative>
  </description>
